*** Resetting replication at the very beginning of the test.

*** Generating a configuration file in JSON format for the Binlog
*** Server utility.

*** Determining binlog file directory from the server.

*** Creating a temporary directory <BINSRV_STORAGE_PATH> for storing
*** binlog files downloaded via the Binlog Server utility.

*** Determining the first binary log name to request from PBS.

*** Shutting down the upstream MySQL server so PBS cannot pull
*** anything and 'binlog_records_' stays empty while the
*** downstream replica connects.

*** Starting Binlog Server Utility in background in pull mode.
*** With the upstream down, PBS enters its reconnect loop and
*** storage stays empty for the whole 'empty' phase of this
*** test.
include/read_file_to_var.inc

*** Waiting for the replication source listener port ready to accept
*** connections.

*** Starting a downstream mysqlbinlog --read-from-remote-server
*** --stop-never session against PBS. --stop-never clears the
*** BINLOG_DUMP_NON_BLOCK flag on the COM_BINLOG_DUMP packet, so
*** PBS must block the session until the requested binlog shows
*** up in storage instead of disconnecting.
include/read_file_to_var.inc

*** Waiting for PBS's log to record that the sender reached the
*** empty-storage polling path. This marker is only written when
*** 'populate_event_block()' takes the EOF branch for an empty
*** storage - pre-fix PBS returned 'false' and 'co_return'ed
*** before ever logging it, so timing out here would itself be
*** a regression of PBS-91.
include/wait_for_pattern_in_file.inc [sender : fetched EOF]

*** Verifying the downstream mysqlbinlog session is still alive
*** while PBS has nothing in storage. Before the PBS-91 fix PBS
*** would have closed the socket as soon as the sender saw an
*** empty storage with a specific binlog name, and mysqlbinlog
*** would have exited within ~1 second.

*** Starting the upstream MySQL server again. PBS's collector
*** thread will notice on its next iteration (idle_time=1s),
*** switch to replication and start populating storage.
# restart

*** Producing a batch of transactions on the upstream source.
CREATE DATABASE test1;
CREATE TABLE test1.t(id INT UNSIGNED NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY) ENGINE=InnoDB;
INSERT INTO test1.t VALUES (1), (2), (3);

*** Waiting for the batch to reach the downstream mysqlbinlog
*** session via PBS. This proves PBS stayed connected to the
*** replica across the empty-storage window and then started
*** delivering events once storage became non-empty.
include/wait_for_pattern_in_file.inc [test1]

*** Sending SIGTERM to the downstream mysqlbinlog session and
*** waiting for it to terminate.

*** Dropping the test database.
DROP DATABASE test1;

*** Sending SIGTERM signal to the Binlog Server Utility and waiting
*** for the process to terminate.

*** Removing the Binlog Server utility storage directory.

*** Removing the Binlog Server utility log file.

*** Removing the Binlog Server utility configuration file.
